  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Find $Xy$ if \n$X=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ -6 & 2\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$y=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}].$",
  "worked_solution": "We multiply each row in the matrix by the column vector using the dot product. Multiplying the first row, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ -6 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5\\cdot 2+(-2)\\cdot 9 \\\\ \u2217\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ \u2217\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying the second row, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ -6 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ (-6)\\cdot 2+2\\cdot 9\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n$Xy=[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].$",
